  "name": "Firecrawl",
  "tagline": "The web data API to search, scrape, and interact at scale",
  "description": "Firecrawl provides a single API that searches, scrapes, crawls, and interacts with the live web, turning any source into clean Markdown or structured data that AI agents can use. Founded in 2022 as part of Y Combinator's Summer 2022 batch by Caleb Peffer, Eric Ciarla, and Nicolas Silberstein Camara, it maintains one of the most-starred open-source crawling projects on GitHub and reports more than 1.25 million developers and 150,000 companies using it. Firecrawl raised a $14.5M Series A led by Nexus Venture Partners in August 2025 and, per an SEC Form D filed in September 2026, sold a further $82 million in preferred stock to seven investors.",
